                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Oleg Drokin &amp;lt;green@whamcloud.com&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2efb5665-d02b-41c5-b0b9-5e12de8ca2ef" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2efb5665-d02b-41c5-b0b9-5e12de8ca2ef&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;br/&gt;
clients: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/113753" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/113753&lt;/a&gt; - 4.18.0-553.50.1.el8_10.x86_64&lt;br/&gt;
servers: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/113753" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/113753&lt;/a&gt; - 4.18.0-553.50.1.el8_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This came in a patch that only changed sait-flr, so I think this is an existing issue in master. potentially some rare race in the test system&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; sanity test_51d: @@@@@@ FAIL: stripecount=3:  OST 2 has more #0 objects vs. OST 1  (154 &amp;gt; 100 x 6/4) &lt;/p&gt;</description>
