                            <comment id="472363" author="emoly.liu" created="Mon, 22 Sep 2025 07:38:31 +0000">&lt;p&gt;+1 on master: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/46fc19bf-5056-4fd5-b2ec-9814adf82185" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/46fc19bf-5056-4fd5-b2ec-9814adf82185&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="472955" author="yujian" created="Thu, 25 Sep 2025 20:00:34 +0000">&lt;p&gt;39 records found in the last 4 weeks.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="475215" author="yujian" created="Thu, 16 Oct 2025 18:56:40 +0000">&lt;p&gt;The sanity/51d subtest passed consistently on the recent master builds in full group test sessions. It only failed sporadically on patch review test sessions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I saw the subtest was improved a couple of times before by the following patches:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/44762" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/44762&lt;/a&gt; ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12058" title="sanity test_51d: @@@@@@ FAIL: OST 1 has less #0 objects vs OST 0 (0 &amp;lt; 1000" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12058"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-12058&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: improve sanity test_51d reliability")&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/48086" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/48086&lt;/a&gt; ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14745" title="sanity:  sanity test_51d: @@@@@@ FAIL: OST 2 has less objects vs OST 1  (134 &amp;lt; 161" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14745"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14745&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: ensure sanity/51d has enough objects")&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/46154" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/46154&lt;/a&gt; ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15282" title="Don't hold a spin locks during space alloc (rr policy)" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15282"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-15282&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: improve sanity test_51d coverage")&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/47978" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/47978&lt;/a&gt; ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15282" title="Don't hold a spin locks during space alloc (rr policy)" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15282"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-15282&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: relax test_51d thresholds somewhat")&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Hi &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=adilger" class="user-hover" rel="adilger"&gt;adilger&lt;/a&gt;, could you please advise if we need to increase the &lt;b&gt;max&lt;/b&gt; value in &lt;tt&gt;test_51d_sub()&lt;/tt&gt; again to relax the threshold?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="475627" author="adilger" created="Tue, 21 Oct 2025 14:59:37 +0000">&lt;p&gt;No, I'm not sure that increasing the max delta is good. At some point the test just becomes meaningless. There is work being done under &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-9" title="Optimize weighted QOS Round-Robin allocator" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-9"&gt;LU-9&lt;/a&gt; that might help this test to be more consistent. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
